@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "AI & Automation";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">AI &amp; Automation</h1>
<p class="text-slate-300 max-w-4xl mb-8">
    I use LLMs, RPA, and lightweight services to remove manual work, surface issues early, and make
    engineering teams faster. Below are representative projects and what they changed.
</p>

<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <!-- Telematics watchdog -->
    <article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-sky-700 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Telematics Replication Watchdog</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">
            Automated monitoring/validation pipeline that
            <strong>increased replication uptime by ~40%</strong> and eliminated weekly outages.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6 text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 marker:text-indigo-400">
            <li>Power Automate flows triggered SQL checks (counts/deltas, integrity between source &amp; target).</li>
            <li>Daily status emails with anomaly detection and drill-down links for fast triage.</li>
            <li>UiPath UI checks verified that data appeared in front-end systems.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="badge-row mt-4">
            <span class="badge">Power Automate</span><span class="badge">UiPath</span>
            <span class="badge">Azure</span><span class="badge">SQL</span>
            <span class="badge">Project Management</span><span class="badge">Stored Procs</span>
        </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Health & status -->
    <article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-sky-700 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Service Health &amp; Deployment Status</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">
            .NET site that aggregates API/DB health and lets business teams post deployment windows/notices—
            a single pane of glass for availability and planned work.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6 text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 marker:text-indigo-400">
            <li>Scheduled health checks calling internal APIs and DB endpoints.</li>
            <li>Admin tools for upcoming maintenance with a visible timeline.</li>
            <li>CI/CD via Azure DevOps/GitHub → Azure App Service; secrets in Key Vault.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="badge-row mt-4">
            <span class="badge">ASP.NET MVC</span><span class="badge">Azure App Service</span>
            <span class="badge">Azure DevOps/GitHub</span><span class="badge">Key Vault</span>
            <span class="badge">C#</span><span class="badge">APIs</span>
        </div>
    </article>

    <!-- RAG assistant -->
    <article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-sky-700 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Resume-aware RAG Chatbot (this site)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">
            OpenAI chat assistant that answers questions about my experience using RAG over my resume/cover letter.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6 text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 marker:text-indigo-400">
            <li>Ingestion: PDFs → chunking → embeddings → vectors stored in SQLite.</li>
            <li>Query: top chunks by cosine similarity → build context → Chat Completions.</li>
            <li>Front-end widget + page view; guarded endpoints with clear errors and quotas.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="badge-row mt-4">
            <span class="badge">OpenAI</span><span class="badge">RAG</span>
            <span class="badge">.NET 8</span><span class="badge">SQLite</span>
            <span class="badge">Tailwind</span>
        </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Dev acceleration -->
    <article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-sky-700 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Developer Acceleration with AI</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">
            Practical AI at the keyboard to move delivery faster and reduce toil.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6 text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 marker:text-indigo-400">
            <li>Copilot/OpenAI for boilerplate generation, test scaffolding, and API-doc summarization.</li>
            <li>Prompt patterns for safe SQL review and “explain-this-diff” to speed code reviews.</li>
            <li>Lightweight scripts to batch-convert logs to structured JSON for ad-hoc analysis.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="badge-row mt-4">
            <span class="badge">GitHub Copilot</span><span class="badge">OpenAI</span>
            <span class="badge">PowerShell</span><span class="badge">.NET</span>
            <span class="badge">Prompting</span>
        </div>
    </article>
</div>

<!-- Other wins -->
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-sky-700 p-5 mt-6">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Other Automations &amp; Patterns</h3>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6 text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 marker:text-indigo-400">
        <li>SQL performance tuning drills with automated baselines and regression compare.</li>
        <li>Release checklists turned into CI tasks (schema drift checks, secret validation, health warm-ups).</li>
        <li>Safety rails around LLM calls: timeouts, retries with back-off, and clear UI errors.</li>
    </ul>
</div>
